As the others have told you and the [s] in the thread subject
indicates, I'm playing Slash'EM.  In Slash'EM, Gehennom is made
considerably more interesting by the fact that it's shorter, all the
named demons have a level of their own (including the big D), there's
no invisible force, and if my impression is correct there's a bit more
variety in the mazes as well.

Shoggoths are like a combination of Green Molds and Ochre Jellies,
except much more powerful.  They hardly move, which makes them easily
avoidable most of the time but all but impossible to go around in
Gehennom.  They are also murder on your equipiment, as they corrode
everything that can be corroded.  Fire Vampires are incorporeal masses
of sentient burning plasma that suck the life out of you in addition
to tossing fireballs around like mad.  Also very annoying.  The black
market is a side level consisting of a gigantic general store with
absurd prices and an absurdly powerful shopkeeper and quite a few
assistants.

The added variety of Slash'EM is great, so long as you don't plan on
winning.

